# Goal Description
This elaborate implementation plan covers the 3-week execution of the "Voice-First ASHA / Health-Worker Co-Pilot" core slice (ASR and RAG). As per the guidelines, this omits LangGraph orchestration and advanced agents, focusing entirely on a demoable, frontend-heavy voice and RAG prototype.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Locking in Tech Stack Choices**
> Please review and confirm the following free/open-source technologies chosen for this project before we begin Phase 0.
> 
> * **Backend & API:** FastAPI (Python), Pydantic for validation.
> * **Frontend:** Next.js (React) for easy UI building and Vercel deployment.
> * **ASR Layer:** Bhashini API (primary for fast Hindi/Tamil/Telugu accuracy) with `faster-whisper` (multilingual) as the local fallback.
> * **Audio Processing:** `torchaudio` and `librosa`.
> * **RAG Vector Store:** ChromaDB (local-first, serverless).
> * **Embeddings:** `paraphrase-multilingual-mpnet-base-v2` via HuggingFace.
> * **RAG Generation LLM:** Groq free-tier API (Llama-3) for speed, with Ollama support as a config flag for fully local generation.
> * **Database (Dev/Prod):** PostgreSQL (via NeonDB).
> * **Deployment:** Local Docker Compose as default; Vercel for frontend demo.

## Proposed Changes (3-Week Implementation Timeline)

The 3-week timeline (approximately 21 Days) is strategically broken down to ensure all phases are completed and thoroughly tested in logical order.

### Week 1: Foundation and Speech (Days 1 - 7)

#### Phase 0: Repo Scaffold & Environment (Days 1 - 2)
*   **[NEW]** Setup Monorepo structure: `backend/`, `frontend/`, `data/`, `eval/`, and `docs/`.
*   **[NEW]** Initialize backend environment (`pyproject.toml` or `requirements.txt`) with pinned dependencies (FastAPI, ChromaDB, etc.).
*   **[NEW]** Initialize Next.js frontend app.
*   **[NEW]** Create `.env.example` mapping out API keys (Groq, Bhashini) and local config flags.
*   **[NEW]** Write `README.md` with simple local run step instructions.

#### Phase 1: Indic Code-Mixed ASR Pipeline (Days 3 - 7)
*   **[NEW]** Implement `POST /asr/transcribe` endpoint in FastAPI.
*   **[NEW]** Build audio preprocessing layer (resampling to 16kHz, mono conversion) using `torchaudio` or `librosa`.
*   **[NEW]** Integrate Bhashini API and `faster-whisper` as swappable inference services.
*   **[NEW]** Download evaluation data (IndicVoices subset, CoSTA code-switched eval sets).
*   **[NEW]** Write eval scripts to calculate WER and CMI-stratified WER.
*   **[NEW]** Output evaluation reports to `/eval/asr_results.json`.

---

### Week 2: Knowledge Retrieval and UI Backbone (Days 8 - 14)

#### Phase 2: RAG System Over NHM/ICMR Protocols (Days 8 - 11)
*   **[NEW]** Source and ingest NHM and ICMR guideline PDFs into the `/data` folder.
*   **[NEW]** Develop PDF text extraction, chunking, and embedding pipeline.
*   **[NEW]** Populate ChromaDB vector index.
*   **[NEW]** Implement `POST /rag/query` FastAPI endpoint returning chunks, generated answers (via Groq/Ollama), and citations.
*   **[NEW]** Create a small curated test set for retrieval-quality bench marking (output to `/eval/`).

#### Phase 3: Frontend Demo Application - Core UI (Days 12 - 14)
*   **[NEW]** Design responsive Next.js standard layout optimized for mobile viewing (large touch targets, simple interface).
*   **[NEW]** Implement "Voice capture panel": in-browser audio recording/upload widget.
*   **[NEW]** Wire up the widget to the `/asr/transcribe` endpoint to display live/near-live transcripts with loading states.

---

### Week 3: UI Completion, Polish, and Handoff (Days 15 - 21)

#### Phase 3: Frontend Demo Application - RAG Integration (Days 15 - 17)
*   **[NEW]** Implement "Protocol assistant panel": chat interface for asking clinical questions.
*   **[NEW]** Wire up chat interface to `/rag/query` and implement source guideline excerpts/expandable UI for trust and verification.
*   **[NEW]** Implement "Visit transcript view": mockup of the future structured protocol snippets view.

#### Phase 4: Integration, Polish & Demo Packaging (Days 18 - 19)
*   **[NEW]** Apply comprehensive error handling, timeout fallbacks, and UI loading states.
*   **[NEW]** Setup Docker Compose to spin up both `backend/` and `frontend/` efficiently.
*   **[NEW]** Write `DEMO.md` detailing a 5-10 minute presentation script.
*   **[NEW]** (Optional) Deploy frontend to Vercel and backend to Render (if time permits).

#### Phase 5: Evaluation Write-Up & Handoff Notes (Days 20 - 21)
*   **[NEW]** Write `/eval/semester_results.md` by consolidating Phase 1 and 2 metrics.
*   **[NEW]** Write `/docs/architecture.md` to document design decisions and tool justifications.
*   **[NEW]** Write `/docs/next_semester.md` defining integration points for LangGraph and the Structuring/Protocol Agents.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
*   **API Tests:** Use `pytest` to run FASTAPI tests to verify `/asr/transcribe` and `/rag/query` schemas load properly and handle empty inputs correctly (e.g. `pytest tests/`).
*   **ASR Evaluation:** Run the Python evaluation scripts for WER and CMI-stratified WER against the CoSTA and IndicVoices subsets appropriately.
*   **RAG Evaluation:** Execute the RAG retrieval-quality check script using the curated expected-document test set.

### Manual Verification
*   **Environment Check:** Run `docker-compose up` to confirm the entire stack runs flawlessly from a fresh clone/restart.
*   **End-to-End Demo Script:** User executes the 5-10 minute script described in `DEMO.md`:
    1.  Navigate to the UI on mobile/desktop via browser.
    2.  Record voice via the Voice Capture Panel.
    3.  Observe transcription output in the Visit Transcript view.
    4.  Query the Protocol Assistant and inspect whether the correct NHM/ICMR citation is returned alongside the generated answer.
